IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Holidays Act 2003 (New Zealand) — THE NOUNS.
--
-- Every fact the rule modules read, and nothing else: no rules, no #EVAL.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2003_129.txt (New Zealand
-- Legislation, version as at 20 December 2023, converted from the PCO XML).
-- Field names are unique across records: L4 cannot tell two records'
-- fields of the same name apart.

§ `Holidays Act 2003 — the nouns`

§§ `Pay (ss 8-10A, 14)`

-- s 14 "gross earnings ... (a) means all payments that the employer is
-- required to pay ... including ... (b) excludes any payments that the
-- employer is not bound ... to pay ... (c) also excludes". One constructor per
-- item the section names.
DECLARE `Payment kind` IS ONE OF
    `(a)(i) salary or wages`
    `(a)(ii) an allowance, other than a non-taxable reimbursement of actual costs`
    `(a)(iii) pay for a holiday or leave taken in the period`
    `(a)(iv) a productivity or incentive-based payment`
    `(a)(v) a payment for overtime`
    `(a)(vi) the cash value of board or lodgings agreed or determined under s 10`
    `(a)(vii) first week compensation under s 97 of the Accident Compensation Act 2001`
    `(b)(i) a discretionary payment`
    `(b)(ii) weekly compensation under the Accident Compensation Act 2001`
    `(b)(iii) a payment for absence on volunteers leave`
    `(c)(i) a reimbursement of actual costs`
    `(c)(ii) a reimbursement of a reasonably assessed amount of costs`
    `(c)(iii) an employer contribution to a superannuation scheme`
    `(c)(iv) a payment for annual holidays paid out under s 28B`
    `s 10A(a) a payment under s 14 of the Home and Community Support Settlement Act 2016`
    `s 10A(b) a payment under s 19 of the Home and Community Support Settlement Act 2016`

DECLARE Payment HAS
    `kind of payment`                                   IS A `Payment kind`
    `amount of the payment`                             IS A NUMBER

-- s 10 "the cash value of any board or lodgings provided by an employer ...
-- (1)(a) as agreed by the employer and employee; or (b) as determined by a
-- Labour Inspector ... (2) ... does not include ... (a) if the work done by
-- the employee requires the employee to stay overnight in a residence other
-- than the employee's usual place of residence; or (b) if the board or
-- lodgings are provided because of special circumstances".
DECLARE `Board or lodgings` HAS
    `cash value agreed or determined`                   IS A NUMBER
    `the work requires staying overnight away from the usual residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provided because of special circumstances`         IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 8 ordinary weekly pay, for annual holiday pay.
DECLARE `Weekly pay facts` HAS
    `it is possible to determine ordinary weekly pay under s 8(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `pay for an ordinary working week`                  IS A NUMBER
    `regular productivity or incentive-based payments`  IS A NUMBER
    `regular overtime`                                  IS A NUMBER
    `board or lodgings in the week`                     IS A MAYBE `Board or lodgings`
    -- s 8(2) a: "gross earnings for (i) the 4 calendar weeks before the end of
    -- the pay period immediately before the calculation is made; or (ii) if
    -- the employee's normal pay period is longer than 4 weeks, that pay period"
    `gross earnings for the s 8(2) period`              IS A NUMBER
    -- s 8(2) b: "the total amount of payments described in subsection
    -- (1)(c)(i) to (iii)" (irregular incentive payments, irregular overtime,
    -- one-off or exceptional payments) in that period.
    `payments described in s 8(1)(c)(i) to (iii) in that period` IS A NUMBER
    `special rate of ordinary weekly pay in the agreement` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- ss 9, 9A relevant daily pay and average daily pay, for public holidays,
-- alternative holidays, sick, bereavement and family violence leave.
DECLARE `Daily pay facts` HAS
    `it is possible and practicable to determine relevant daily pay` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9(1)(a)-(b): what the employee would have received had they worked
    -- the day, with the incentive and overtime payments they would have
    -- received, and without any time-and-a-half added by s 50(1)(a) (s 9(2)).
    `pay the employee would have received had they worked the day` IS A NUMBER
    `board or lodgings on the day`                      IS A MAYBE `Board or lodgings`
    `special rate of relevant daily pay in the agreement` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the employee's daily pay varies within the pay period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer chooses average daily pay`            IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9A(2) a: "gross earnings for the 52 calendar weeks before the end of
    -- the pay period immediately before the calculation is made".
    `gross earnings for the 52 weeks before the last pay period ended` IS A NUMBER
    -- s 9A(2) b: "the number of whole or part days during which the employee
    -- earned those gross earnings, including any day on which the employee
    -- was on a paid holiday or paid leave".
    `whole or part days on which those earnings were earned` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Continuous employment (ss 16(2)-(3), 85)`

-- s 16(2) "(a) includes any period during which the employee was— (i) on paid
-- holidays or leave under this Act ...; (ii) on parental leave ...; (iii) on
-- volunteers leave ...; (iv) receiving weekly compensation ...; (v) on unpaid
-- sick leave or unpaid bereavement leave or unpaid family violence leave;
-- or (vi) on unpaid leave for any other reason for a period of no more than
-- 1 week; but (b) unless otherwise agreed, does not include any other unpaid
-- leave".
DECLARE `Kind of absence` IS ONE OF
    `(a)(i) paid holidays or leave under this Act`
    `(a)(ii) parental leave`
    `(a)(iii) volunteers leave`
    `(a)(iv) receiving weekly compensation under the Accident Compensation Act 2001`
    `(a)(v) unpaid sick, bereavement or family violence leave`
    `other unpaid leave`

DECLARE Absence HAS
    `kind of absence`                                   IS A `Kind of absence`
    `length in days`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `agreed to be included in the 12 months`            IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Annual holidays (ss 16-40)`

-- ss 27, 28, 28B, 55, 60, 61, 72, 72J: when a payment must be made.
DECLARE `When payment is due` IS ONE OF
    `before the holiday is taken`
    `in the pay for the period in which the holiday is taken`
    `in the pay for the final period of employment`
    `in the pay for the pay period in which the holiday or leave falls`
    `as soon as practicable after the employer agrees`
    `with the employee's pay, as an identifiable component`
    `when the employee produces the proof required`
    `nothing is payable`

-- s 21-22: an annual holiday taken.
DECLARE `Annual holiday` HAS
    `holiday begins on`                                 IS A DATE
    `portion taken, in weeks`                           IS A NUMBER
    `taken in advance of the entitlement`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `employment began on`                               IS A DATE
    `weekly pay at the beginning of the holiday`        IS A `Weekly pay facts`
    -- s 21(2)(b)(ii) and s 22(2)(b)(ii)(A): the 12 months before the end of
    -- the last pay period before the holiday; s 22(2)(b)(ii)(B): the period of
    -- employment before then, if less than 12 months.
    `last pay period before the holiday ended on`       IS A DATE
    `gross earnings over the averaging period`          IS A NUMBER
    `absences in the averaging period`                  IS A LIST OF Absence

-- ss 23-26, 40(2)-(3), 60(2)(b): the end of the employment.
DECLARE `End of employment` HAS
    `employment ended on`                               IS A DATE
    `employment commenced on`                           IS A DATE
    `the employee has become entitled to annual holidays` IS A BOOLEAN
    `weeks of annual holidays entitlement not taken`    IS A NUMBER
    `weekly pay at the end`                             IS A `Weekly pay facts`
    `gross earnings in the 12 months before the last pay period ended` IS A NUMBER
    `absences in those 12 months`                       IS A LIST OF Absence
    -- s 23(2), s 25(2): "gross earnings since the commencement of employment"
    -- or "since the employee last became entitled to the annual holidays".
    `gross earnings since commencement or since the last entitlement` IS A NUMBER
    `paid for annual holidays taken in advance`         IS A NUMBER
    `paid with the employee's pay under s 28`           IS A NUMBER
    -- s 40(3): the public holidays that would have fallen in the remaining
    -- annual holidays, had they been taken immediately after the end.
    `public holidays in the notional holiday on otherwise working days` IS A NUMBER
    `alternative holidays not taken`                    IS A NUMBER
    `daily pay on the last day of employment`           IS A `Daily pay facts`

-- s 28: paying annual holiday pay with the employee's pay.
DECLARE `Pay-as-you-go basis` IS ONE OF
    `(a)(i) a fixed-term agreement to work for less than 12 months`
    `(a)(ii) work so intermittent or irregular that 4 weeks' holidays are impracticable`
    `neither`

DECLARE `Pay-as-you-go arrangement` HAS
    `basis of the employment`                           IS A `Pay-as-you-go basis`
    `the employee agrees in the employment agreement`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid as an identifiable component of pay`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `percentage of gross earnings paid`                 IS A NUMBER

-- ss 28A-28F: cashing up annual holidays.
DECLARE `Payout request` HAS
    `request made in writing`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `weeks requested to be paid out`                    IS A NUMBER
    `weeks already paid out in the entitlement year`    IS A NUMBER
    `a policy under s 28E covers that part of the business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer agrees to the request`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `weekly pay when the request is agreed`             IS A `Weekly pay facts`
    `gross earnings in the 12 months before agreement`  IS A NUMBER
    -- s 28A(1): "a portion of the employee's entitlement to annual holidays".
    `weeks of current annual holidays entitlement not taken` IS A NUMBER
    `absences in the 12 months before agreement`        IS A LIST OF Absence

-- ss 29-35: a closedown.
DECLARE Closedown HAS
    `closedown begins on`                               IS A DATE
    `notice of the closedown given on`                  IS A DATE
    `another closedown in the same 12 months`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `employee entitled to annual holidays at the commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `weeks of closedown on otherwise working days`      IS A NUMBER
    `weeks of annual holidays entitlement available`    IS A NUMBER
    `agreed to take the rest in advance (s 33(3))`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `weekly pay at the closedown`                       IS A `Weekly pay facts`
    `gross earnings in the 12 months before the closedown` IS A NUMBER
    `gross earnings since commencement or last entitlement, at the closedown` IS A NUMBER
    `advance holiday pay already paid`                  IS A NUMBER
    `pay-as-you-go holiday pay already paid`            IS A NUMBER
    `absences in the 12 months before the closedown`    IS A LIST OF Absence

-- ss 36-39: a sickness, injury, bereavement or family violence arising
-- during, or before, scheduled annual holidays, or after other leave runs out.
DECLARE `Clash with annual holidays` IS ONE OF
    `s 36 sick or injured, or a spouse, partner or dependant is, during annual holidays`
    `s 37 a bereavement during annual holidays`
    `s 37A family violence leave becomes available during annual holidays`
    `s 38 any of these before scheduled annual holidays`
    `s 39 sick, bereavement or family violence leave exhausted`

§§ `Public holidays (ss 44-61A)`

-- s 44(1). Matariki Observance Day and the anniversary day are inputs:
-- Schedule 1 of the Te Kāhui o Matariki Public Holiday Act 2022 sets the
-- one, and local observance the other.
DECLARE `Public holiday` IS ONE OF
    `(a) Christmas Day`
    `(b) Boxing Day`
    `(c) New Year's Day`
    `(d) 2 January`
    `Waitangi Day`
    `Good Friday`
    `Easter Monday`
    `ANZAC Day`
    `the Sovereign's birthday`
    `Matariki Observance Day`
    `Labour Day`
    `the anniversary of a province`

DECLARE `Calendar inputs` HAS
    `calendar year`                                     IS A NUMBER
    `Matariki Observance Day that year`                 IS A DATE
    `anniversary day observed locally that year`        IS A DATE
    -- s 12: the weekdays the employee would otherwise work (0 Sunday ...
    -- 6 Saturday, as in the daydate library).
    `weekdays the employee would otherwise work`        IS A LIST OF NUMBER

-- s 59: being on call on a public holiday.
DECLARE `On call` IS ONE OF
    `not on call`
    `(2) on call and called in to work`
    `(3) on call, not called in, and for all practical purposes not a whole holiday`
    `(3) on call, not called in, and had a whole holiday`

-- s 61A: why an employee who was to work did not.
DECLARE `Reason for not working` IS ONE OF
    `(a) sick or injured, or a spouse, partner or dependant is`
    `(b) a bereavement under s 69(2)`
    `(c) entitled to family violence leave under s 72C`
    `any other reason`

-- One public holiday, as it fell for the employee (after any transfer
-- under s 44A or 44B, and after ss 45, 45A).
DECLARE `Public holiday worked or not` HAS
    `the public holiday falls on`                       IS A DATE
    `would otherwise be a working day for the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee worked any part of the day under the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee was required or had agreed to work`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `reason the employee did not work`                  IS A `Reason for not working`
    `works for the employer only on public holidays`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `on call status`                                    IS AN `On call`
    `daily pay for the public holiday`                  IS A `Daily pay facts`
    -- s 50(1)(a): "the portion of the employee's relevant daily pay or
    -- average daily pay (less any penal rates) that relates to the time
    -- actually worked"; (b): "the portion of the employee's relevant daily
    -- pay that relates to the time actually worked".
    `portion of the daily pay for the time actually worked` IS A NUMBER
    `penal rates within that portion`                   IS A NUMBER
    `portion of relevant daily pay for the time actually worked` IS A NUMBER

-- s 44B: an agreement to transfer a whole public holiday.
DECLARE `Whole transfer` HAS
    `agreed in writing`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the public holiday is identified`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the public holiday would otherwise be a working day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the new day is identified or identifiable`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the new day would otherwise be a working day`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the new day is another public holiday or part of one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the purpose is to avoid the entitlements under ss 50 and 56` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a policy under s 44C covers that part of the business for the whole transfer` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 44A: an agreement to transfer part of a public holiday.
DECLARE `Part transfer` HAS
    `the employee starts work on one day and finishes on the next` IS A BOOLEAN
    `one or both days are public holidays`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `part transfer agreed in writing`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `each 24-hour period starts or finishes on the public holiday and covers the shift` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the purpose of the part transfer is to avoid the entitlements under ss 50 and 56` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a policy under s 44C covers that part of the business for the part transfer` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 57: taking an alternative holiday.
DECLARE `Alternative holiday` HAS
    `alternative holiday taken on`                      IS A DATE
    `the day was agreed`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day would otherwise be a working day`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `a whole working day off`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day is a public holiday`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice of the day given on`                        IS A MAYBE DATE
    `daily pay on the alternative holiday`              IS A `Daily pay facts`

-- s 61: exchanging an alternative holiday for payment.
DECLARE `Exchange request` HAS
    `entitlement to the alternative holiday arose on`   IS A DATE
    `exchange requested on`                             IS A DATE
    `the employer agrees to exchange`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount agreed in exchange`                         IS A NUMBER

§§ `Sick, bereavement and family violence leave (ss 63-72J)`

-- ss 63(1), 72D(1): when the entitlement first arises.
DECLARE Service HAS
    `current continuous employment began on`            IS A DATE
    -- s 63(1)(b), s 72D(1)(b): "over a period of 6 months, worked for the
    -- employer for (i) at least an average of 10 hours a week ...; and (ii)
    -- no less than 1 hour in every week ... or no less than 40 hours in every
    -- month". The last day of the first such 6 months, if any.
    `the hours test was first met over 6 months ending on` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the hours test still applies`                      IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Leave kind` IS ONE OF
    `sick leave`
    `bereavement leave`
    `family violence leave`

-- s 65(1).
DECLARE `Whose sickness` IS ONE OF
    `(a) the employee is sick or injured`
    `(b) the employee's spouse or partner is sick or injured`
    `(c) a person who depends on the employee for care is sick or injured`
    `someone else`

-- s 69(2).
DECLARE Bereavement IS ONE OF
    `(a) the death of a spouse or partner, parent, child, brother or sister, grandparent, grandchild, or spouse's or partner's parent`
    `(b) the death of another person, if the employer accepts the employee has suffered a bereavement`
    `(b) the death of another person, if the employer does not accept it`
    `(c) the end of the employee's pregnancy by miscarriage or still-birth`
    `(d) the end of another person's pregnancy by miscarriage or still-birth, for a spouse, partner, intended parent or primary carer`
    `(d) the end of another person's pregnancy, for anyone else`

-- s 72B: a person affected by family violence.
DECLARE `Family violence facts` HAS
    `family violence is inflicted, or has been inflicted, on the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a child against whom family violence is or was inflicted resides with the person` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A spell of sick, bereavement or family violence leave.
DECLARE Leave HAS
    `kind of leave`                                     IS A `Leave kind`
    `leave begins on`                                   IS A DATE
    `service`                                           IS A Service
    `days of leave on otherwise working days`           IS A NUMBER
    `days left in the current entitlement`              IS A NUMBER
    `agreed to take leave in advance`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `whose sickness or injury`                          IS A `Whose sickness`
    `bereavements`                                      IS A LIST OF Bereavement
    `family violence`                                   IS A `Family violence facts`
    `daily pay for the leave`                           IS A `Daily pay facts`
    `days for which ACC weekly compensation is paid`    IS A NUMBER
    `proof was required and not produced without reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 68: requiring proof of sickness or injury.
DECLARE `Proof request` HAS
    `consecutive calendar days of sickness or injury`   IS A NUMBER
    `the employer informed the employee as early as possible` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer agrees to meet reasonable expenses`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the leave is beyond the s 65 entitlement and proof was agreed` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Enforcement (ss 74-85)`

DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a company or other body corporate`

DECLARE Enforcer IS ONE OF
    `(a) the employee`
    `(b) an authorised representative`
    `(c) a representative of the employee's union`
    `(d) an employer`
    `(e) a Labour Inspector`

-- s 75(2): the provisions whose breach attracts a penalty, in the order
-- the subsection lists them.
DECLARE `Provision breached` IS ONE OF
    `s 16 or ss 21 to 28`
    `s 40(3)`
    `ss 28A and 28B`
    `s 46, ss 49 to 56, s 60 or s 61(3)`
    `s 63, s 65 or ss 69 to 72`
    `s 72C or ss 72H to 72J`
    `s 81`
    `s 82`
    `another provision`

-- s 81(2): the holiday and leave record, one flag per item kept.
DECLARE `Holiday and leave record` HAS
    `name`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `date employment commenced`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours worked each day in a pay period and the pay for them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `current entitlement to annual holidays`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `date last entitled to annual holidays`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `current entitlement to sick leave`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `dates of annual holidays and leave taken`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment for annual holidays and leave taken`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `portion of annual holidays paid out`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `date and amount of each payout`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `dates of, and payments for, public holidays worked` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours worked on public holidays`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `public holidays transferred and the days they went to` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of entitlement to each alternative holiday` IS A BOOLEAN
    `public and alternative holidays not worked but paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cash value of board or lodgings`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `payments in exchange for alternative holidays` IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of termination`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `holiday pay paid on termination`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `kept in written form, or convertible into it`      IS A BOOLEAN
